From ac23eb4540abe65e0a56067b7fb06fada45cd89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:48:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/27] feat(renderer): polygonal bokeh and aperture
 diffraction streaks

- Gather DOF: restore the amputated circle-to-polygon kernel blend
  (round wide open, full n-gon by f/8) and feed real lens values via new
  Dof_User_ApertureBlades / Dof_User_FNumber post params instead of the
  hardcoded 8/8.
- Diffraction streaks (sunstars) at the end of the bloom stage: soft-
  knee threshold at quarter res, then symmetric line stretches - each
  pass paints two opposed collinear spikes, so even blade counts give N
  spikes and odd give 2N (up to 24) with half as many passes. Spike
  length is governed by per-tap decay (0.55-0.95) plus stride, so
  stopping down reads as the spikes growing rather than fading in.
  Output compensates the tonemapper's bloom composite weight so streak
  energy is independent of the scene's Bloom amount. Zero new render
  targets (reuses the bloom scratch chain); r_HDRStreaks cvar (0 off,
  1 on, 2 diagnostic force mode) early-outs completely when disabled.
- HDRStreaks post effect (HDR_Streaks_* params) follows the CDepthOfField
  container pattern; spike-count clamp 4..24 end to end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
